      "content": "The wealth gap has exploded primarily because corporate tax cuts and deregulation have allowed the ultra-wealthy to accumulate capital at an unprecedented rate while wages for average workers have stagnated. This concentration of power in the hands of a few has distorted the economy, driving up housing costs and making it nearly impossible for middle-class families to compete. The solution isn't just tweaking policies but fundamentally restructuring our tax code to ensure the wealthy pay their fair share and reinvest that money into public infrastructure and education.",
      "source": "target",
